From: zyi
Subject: [PATCH] standby: hard 5 s wake blackout, record wake source (debug)

Every board run woke ~0.13 s after entering deep standby, always inside
the clk_suspend/clk_resume window (the "wakeup: %d" print lands in the
UART divider change and is lost in garble), even with ehci1/ohci1
unbound, the R-PIO registration refused, and the same-second RTC_HMS
de-glitch in place (the exit still ran 0.12 s after the DRAM save, so
the impostor was accepted as a later-second wake -- it lands after
wait_wakeup captured its reference second, or the HMS readback is not
reliable). Hard blackout instead: ignore every wake for the first 5 s
after entry (nothing on this board legitimately wakes that early -- the
tests wake by RTC alarm at +20 s and the power key sits on the PMU NMI).
Ignored wakes are recorded in the always-on RTC_GPR0 (0xED000000|src) /
RTC_GPR1 (age in ticks) and survive a warm reboot; accepted wakes print
readably and record as 0xEE000000|src. standby_init prints the previous
attempt's record.

--- a/ar100s/service/standby/standby-sun60iw2p1/plat_standby.c
+++ b/ar100s/service/standby/standby-sun60iw2p1/plat_standby.c
@@ -322,9 +322,12 @@
 
 static void wait_wakeup(void)
 {
+	u32 t_entry;
+
 	save_state_flag(REC_ESTANDBY | REC_WAIT_WAKEUP | 0x01);
 	wakeup_timer_start();
 	//wakeup_source = NO_WAKESOURCE;
+	t_entry = current_time_tick();
 	while (1) {
 		/*
 		 * maybe add user defined task process here
@@ -332,7 +335,31 @@
 
 
 		if (wakeup_source != NO_WAKESOURCE) {
-			LOG("wakeup: %d\n", wakeup_source);
+			/*
+			 * De-glitch (debug, hard blackout): every board run so far
+			 * woke ~0.13 s after entry, inside the clk_suspend/
+			 * clk_resume window where the UART divider is mid-change.
+			 * Whatever the impostor is (clock-switch noise, PMU NMI
+			 * line state), nothing on this board can legitimately
+			 * request a wake within the first 5 s of the entry
+			 * sequence (our tests wake by RTC alarm at +20 s; the
+			 * power key sits on the PMU NMI, not here). Ignore and
+			 * record everything in that window in the always-on
+			 * RTC_GPR0 (source) / RTC_GPR1 (age in ticks); a wake
+			 * after 5 s is accepted.
+			 */
+			u32 age = current_time_tick() - t_entry;
+
+			if (age < 5 * TICK_PER_SEC) {
+				writel(0xED000000u | wakeup_source, RTC_GPR0);
+				writel(age, RTC_GPR1);
+				LOG("ignore early wake %d age %d\n", wakeup_source, age);
+				wakeup_source = NO_WAKESOURCE;
+				continue;
+			}
+			writel(0xEE000000u | wakeup_source, RTC_GPR0);
+			writel(age, RTC_GPR1);
+			LOG("wake src: %d age %d\n", wakeup_source, age);
 			break;
 		}
 		/* e902 low power mode */
--- a/ar100s/service/standby/standby.c
+++ b/ar100s/service/standby/standby.c
@@ -41,6 +41,11 @@
 
 	wakeup_timer_init();
 
+	/* debug: wake-source records of the previous standby attempt
+	 * (0xED/0xEE000000|src in RTC_GPR0, see plat_standby.c); survives a
+	 * warm reboot, cleared by a full power cut. */
+	LOG("last wake record: %x\n", readl(RTC_GPR0));
+
 	return OK;
 }
 
